   "definition_quote": "We consider a K-armed bandit ... the expected revenue of each arm scales linearly in T, namely, \\forall k: E[sum_t r_t I(A_t = k)] >= \\lambda_k T ... The total per-round excess-regret and constraint violation are respectively defined by R_T = sum_k Delta_k E[sum_t (p_{k,t} - p*_k)_+], and V_T = sum_k mu_k E[sum_t (p*_k - p_{k,t})_+]. Assumption 1: F is the family of 1-sub-Gaussian distributions."
